<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladimir Yaroslavich of Galicia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1151–1199</span> · Also known as Volodymyr Yaroslavych</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladimir Yaroslavich was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-osmomysl">Yaroslav Osmomysl</a>. Driven out by his boyars and briefly ousted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1188, he regained Halych with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. His death in 1199 ended the local dynasty, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-the-great">Roman Mstislavich</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a> took Galicia.</p></div>
